WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:03.820
Another troubleshooting tool to use is a cable
tester.

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:08.109
With a cable tester, one can plug both ends
of an Ethernet cable into the tester and learn

00:00:08.109 --> 00:00:11.890
two things about the cable: first, whether
it is a straight-through or crossover cable

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:16.480
and, secondly, whether there is a break in
the cable, as we cannot always see a physical

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:17.890
break in a cable.

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:22.869
This tool can help identify which cables need
to be redone or replaced and, if you have

00:00:22.869 --> 00:00:27.230
a bad network connection and the cable itself
is fine, start looking at other causes of

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:28.070
the bad connection.

